<title>USA: Lakehead to expand crude pipeline capacity.</title>
<headline>Lakehead to expand crude pipeline capacity.</headline>
<dateline>DULUTH, Minn. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lakehead Pipe Line Partners LP on Thursday said it planned a four-stage program to increase Western Canadian crude oil pipeline capacity in conjunction with its IPL Energy Inc affiliate.</p>
<p>The project, expected to cost C$875 million, could ultimately provide an additional 520,000 barrels of crude oil per day, Lakehead said.</p>
<p>Lakehead owns the U.S. portion of the world's longest liquid petroleum pipeline.</p>
<p>Its shares were off 1/8 at 35-3/4 early Thursday afternoon.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
